      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The notion that you must compromise your integrity to participate is a false choice designed to paralyze the electorate. While no candidate is perfect, abstaining simply validates the status quo and allows the morally objectionable to win by default. Your personal integrity is best upheld not by sitting on the sidelines, but by actively choosing the *least* objectionable path available to hold power accountable.",
      "source": "target",
